      "sequence_position": 1,
      "problem": "Given that $P(K|L)=0.25,$ $P(K)=0.75,$ and $P(L)=0.3,$ compute $P(L|K).$",
      "worked_solution": "Using Bayes' theorem, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}P(L|K) & =\\frac{P(K|L)P(L)}{P(K)} \\\\  & =\\frac{(0.25)(0.3)}{0.75} \\\\  & =\\frac{0.075}{0.75} \\\\  & =0.1.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
